116:- **Theme poles** (#1224) — `light_theme` / `dark_theme`, one daisyUI theme each, from
117:  `App\Support\ThemeFamilies` (light: `light, cupcake, fantasy`; dark: `dark, synthwave, coffee,
118:  luxury`; defaults `fantasy`/`dark`). The header `<x-theme-toggle>` cycles between exactly those
124:**Enabling a daisyUI theme** touches four places that must agree (`ThemeFamilies` is the source of
127:1. `ThemeFamilies::LIGHT`/`DARK` + `LABELS` — validation, the two selects, the toggle;
128:2. `resources/css/app.css` — the `themes:` list, the `@custom-variant dark` selector list when it is a
129:   dark pole, the `[data-theme=…] .stitch-bg-fixed` group, and the `:not([data-theme=…])` blob chain.
131:   backdrop (2.60:1) — the #1224 sweep caught it;
132:3. `THEMES` in `tests/e2e/theme/theme-helpers.ts`;
133:4. `tests/e2e/theme/sweep.spec.ts` fails on any sub-threshold surface, so the table stays honest.
135:The split is measured, not aesthetic: daisyUI declares `color-scheme` per theme, and the e2e suite
136:asserts each select's options agree with their theme's own `color-scheme`.
